 "segments": [
  {
   "start": 0.2,
   "end": 0.92,
   "text": "Meet the groma."
  },
  {
   "start": 1.2,
   "end": 5.7,
   "text": "It's a pole with a wooden cross on top, and four weights hanging from strings."
  },
  {
   "start": 6.04,
   "end": 6.52,
   "text": "That's it."
  },
  {
   "start": 6.8,
   "end": 7.58,
   "text": "No lenses."
  },
  {
   "start": 7.84,
   "end": 8.62,
   "text": "No compass."
  },
  {
   "start": 8.88,
   "end": 9.64,
   "text": "No GPS."
  },
  {
   "start": 9.94,
   "end": 12.62,
   "text": "The strings hang straight down because of gravity."
  },
  {
   "start": 12.94,
   "end": 18.46,
   "text": "So when Marcus lines up two strings with his eye, he gets a perfectly straight line of sight."
  },
  {
   "start": 18.74,
   "end": 21.14,
   "text": "An assistant walks ahead with a tall pole."
  },
  {
   "start": 21.52,
   "end": 21.9,
   "text": "Left."
  },
  {
   "start": 22.16,
   "end": 22.54,
   "text": "Left."
  },
  {
   "start": 22.84,
   "end": 23.24,
   "text": "Stop!\""
  },
  {
   "start": 23.72,
   "end": 25.58,
   "text": "Plant it. Then another pole,"
  },
  {
   "start": 25.78,
   "end": 26.46,
   "text": "further on."
  },
  {
   "start": 26.74,
   "end": 29.52,
   "text": "When all the poles line up, they hide each other."
  },
  {
   "start": 29.8,
   "end": 31.14,
   "text": "You see just one pole."
  },
  {
   "start": 31.46,
   "end": 33.5,
   "text": "That's how you know the line is straight."
  },
  {
   "start": 33.78,
   "end": 34.7,
   "text": "Here's the catch."
  },
  {
   "start": 34.98,
   "end": 37.52,
   "text": "This tool is brilliant at exactly one thing."
  },
  {
   "start": 37.8,
   "end": 38.68,
   "text": "Straight lines."
  },
  {
   "start": 38.96,
   "end": 39.98,
   "text": "Now scale it up."
  },
  {
   "start": 40.3,
   "end": 44.74,
   "text": "To link two forts many miles apart, surveyors couldn't see one from the other."
  },
  {
   "start": 45.02,
   "end": 48.2,
   "text": "So, historians think, they worked from high ground."
  },
  {
   "start": 48.48,
   "end": 50.56,
   "text": "A fire or a pole on one hilltop."
  },
  {
   "start": 50.84,
   "end": 54.06,
   "text": "Another on the next. Smoke by day, flames by night."
  },
  {
   "start": 54.38,
   "end": 55.86,
   "text": "Then they filled in the gaps,"
  },
  {
   "start": 56.06,
   "end": 59.28,
   "text": "pole by pole. The result is not one perfect line."
  },
  {
   "start": 59.54,
   "end": 63.78,
   "text": "It's a chain of straight segments, and each one bends a little at a hilltop."
  },
  {
   "start": 64.08,
   "end": 65.74,
   "text": "Look at the Fosse Way in Britain."
  },
  {
   "start": 66.02,
   "end": 69.64,
   "text": "It runs about two hundred miles, from Lincoln down to Devon."
  },
  {
   "start": 69.9,
   "end": 74.42,
   "text": "And yet it never strays more than about six miles from a single straight line."
  },
  {
   "start": 74.7,
   "end": 77.28,
   "text": "Not bad for sticks, string, and smoke. Bran's goat,"
  },
  {
   "start": 77.56,
   "end": 81.34,
   "text": "meanwhile, has walked three miles and gotten nowhere."
  },
  {
   "start": 81.64,
   "end": 83.08,
   "text": "So here's the real answer."
  },
  {
   "start": 83.34,
   "end": 87.2,
   "text": "Roman roads were straight because straight was the easiest thing to survey."
  },
  {
   "start": 87.52,
   "end": 88.84,
   "text": "With a groma and poles,"
  },
  {
   "start": 89.02,
   "end": 92.48,
   "text": "a straight line is simple and almost impossible to get wrong."
  },
  {
   "start": 92.78,
   "end": 93.64,
   "text": "A smooth curve?"
  },
  {
   "start": 93.92,
   "end": 97.86,
   "text": "That takes far more measuring, and good maps they mostly didn't have."
  },
  {
   "start": 98.16,
   "end": 99.04,
   "text": "Then add power."
  },
  {
   "start": 99.32,
   "end": 106.7,
   "text": "Rome had soldiers to do the digging, and it rarely asked conquered locals for permission. Bogs got filled with timber and stone."
  },
  {
   "start": 106.98,
   "end": 110.92,
   "text": "Back at the swamp, the soldiers start sinking logs into the mud."
  },
  {
   "start": 111.2,
   "end": 112.2,
   "text": "Rivers got bridges."
  },
  {
   "start": 112.5,
   "end": 119.36,
   "text": "And when a hill was truly too steep for carts and mules, the surveyors gave up on straight and zigzagged up the slope."
  },
  {
   "start": 119.64,
   "end": 120.96,
   "text": "Straight wasn't a religion."
  },
  {
   "start": 121.22,
   "end": 123.12,
   "text": "It was the default setting of the tool."
  },
  {
   "start": 123.42,
   "end": 124.84,
   "text": "So Bran was half right."
  },
  {
   "start": 125.1,
   "end": 127.0,
   "text": "And those lines outlived the empire."
  },
  {
   "start": 127.28,
   "end": 130.78,
   "text": "In Britain, modern roads still run on top of Roman routes,"
  },
  {
   "start": 130.96,
   "end": 134.48,
   "text": "like Watling Street, now under long stretches of the A5."
  },
  {
   "start": 134.78,
   "end": 138.72,
   "text": "Drive them today and you'll feel it: the road just refuses to turn."
  },
  {
   "start": 139.02,
   "end": 142.18,
   "text": "Meanwhile, back at the swamp, the new road is finished."
  },
  {
   "start": 142.48,
   "end": 143.52,
   "text": "Marcus walks it,"
  },
  {
   "start": 143.7,
   "end": 144.1,
   "text": "proud."
  },
  {
   "start": 144.38,
   "end": 145.9,
   "text": "The centurion marches by,"
  },
  {
   "start": 146.08,
   "end": 146.96,
   "text": "dry for once."
  },
  {
   "start": 147.22,
   "end": 148.12,
   "text": "And Bran's goat?"
  },
  {
   "start": 148.42,
   "end": 150.34,
   "text": "It stops at the edge of the stone."
  },
  {
   "start": 150.64,
   "end": 152.82,
   "text": "Looks left at its winding old path."
  },
  {
   "start": 153.1,
   "end": 154.42,
   "text": "Looks right at the road."
  },
  {
   "start": 154.7,
   "end": 156.46,
   "text": "And trots straight down the middle."
  },
  {
   "start": 156.8,
   "end": 158.8,
   "text": "So why were Roman roads so straight?"
  },
  {
   "start": 159.08,
   "end": 162.08,
   "text": "Because a stick and some string could only see straight."
  },
  {
   "start": 162.36,
   "end": 165.62,
   "text": "And Rome was stubborn enough to build whatever the stick saw."
  }
 ],
